{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Ban all alternative remittance systems to disrupt small boat smuggling networks",
        "additional_details": "Channel people-smuggling syndicates rely heavily on informal brokers to act as a trusted escrow mechanism. These operators hold a migrant\u2019s cash in front businesses\u2014like tech repair shops or mini-mart. Current regulations require lengthy financial investigations to prove money laundering before a shop can be shut down. A total ban on these parallel ledgers could help allow the National Crime Agency and Border Security Command to dismantle local cash networks funding small boat logistics.",
        "background": "Introduce a total statutory ban on alternative remittance systems such as the hawala banking system and parallel remittance ledgers. Operating or participating in an informal, trust-based money network must be made a criminal offence to force the closure of shops acting as physical cash hubs.",
